# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every OS.
#
# Without this file, a clone on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` (git's own
# Windows default) checks every file out with CRLF, and `npm run format:check`
# then fails on all 148 of them — Prettier's `endOfLine` is "lf". The suite is
# green, the code is untouched, and the verify gate can never pass locally.
# `eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf`, so the checkout matches what CI sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The app icons and splash art. `text=auto` would detect these anyway; saying so
# explicitly means a future binary format never depends on that detection.
*.png binary
